@startuml sources-recommended-sequence
!include ../../_style/sequence.iuml
title Sources > Recommended — listed with the AI's check, then added by their id

actor Reader
participant RecommendedSources as Page
participant "feedRouter\n+ feedController" as Router
participant recommendationService as Service
participant "feedbackService\n+ sourceService" as Known
participant "profileModel\n+ feedModel" as Models
participant "profileAi\n(confirmOnSubject)" as AI
participant "ollama\n(gemma4:31b)" as Ollama
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Listed ==

Reader -> Page : opens the profile page
Page -> Router : GET /feeds/recommended (X-Profile)
Router -> Service : list(profileId)
Service -> Models : get(profileId) (none: [])
par
    Service -> Known : FeedbackService.of: the feeds the thumbs left out
else
    Service -> Models : removedSources, userFeedUrls, interests
end
Service -> Known : knownMedia(profileId, {userFeeds: own + removed})
Service -> Models : recommendedFeeds(profileId, {excluded: shared\n+ refused + removed, since 7 days, 0.45,\n3 relevant, 2%, limit 60, 12 titles})
Models -> DB : the other profiles' feeds, their news of 7 days\nscored on the interests (title vectors)
Service -> Service : left out: looksPrivate(url), and a medium\nthe reader already reads (nameOf(siteOf(url)))
loop 4 candidates at a time, until 20 kept
    Service -> Service : confirmed(profileId, interests, row):\nthe verdict kept 24 h, same interests
    opt not kept yet
        Service -> AI : confirmOnSubject(interests, 12 titles)
        AI -> Ollama : ollamaJson(confirmPrompt)
        Ollama --> AI : {onSubject: [numbers]}
        AI --> Service : the titles confirmed (null: no answer)
    end
    Service -> Service : afterConfirmation: relevant = relevant x\nconfirmed / judged; under 3 or 2% of its\nnews: left out; null verdict: kept as is
end
Service --> Page : 20 at most, the most relevant first:\n[{id, site, url (null on the bridge), category,\nlanguage, news, relevant, samples}]

== Added ==

Reader -> Page : "Add" or "Add all n"
Page -> Router : POST /feeds/recommended {ids} (needsProfile)
Router -> Service : add(userId, profileId, ids)
Service -> Service : 1 to 20 integer ids (else 400)
Service -> Service : recommended(profileId) again:\nonly an id still offered is added
Service -> Models : countUserFeeds, userFeedUrls
loop each id
    alt not offered any more, 800 sources, no room on the bridge
        Service -> Service : an error for this id
    else
        Service -> Models : addUserFeed(url of the server's row,\nsite, category, language): origin 'user'
    end
end
Service --> Page : {feeds, errors}
Page --> Reader : added to "Your sources", the others stay
@enduml
